{{#step}}
Create the R2 bucket that holds the media and the page cache, declining Wrangler's offer to add the binding itself as in step 1:

   {{> cloudflare/r2-bucket}}
{{/step}}
{{#step}}
Create the bucket of the backups. Only the cron Worker binds it, so the Worker that serves the public media cannot read them:

   {{> cloudflare/r2-bucket-command suffix="backups"}}
{{/step}}
{{#step}}
Migrate the local database again, create its admin (from `apps/web/.env.admin`) and seed it. Local data is keyed by the `database_id`, so the real id switches local development to a new, empty database: until it is migrated, requests fail with `no such table`.

   ```bash
   {{runScript "migrate"}}
   {{runScript "ensure-admin"}}
   {{runScript "db:seed"}}
   ```
{{/step}}
